# Do NOT create .sandcastle/.env. Sandcastle forwards every key in it into
# the sandbox, whichever agent runs, and the scripts refuse to start if it
# holds any keys.
#
# Where credentials come from, highest first:
#   1. A 1Password Environment, when OP_ENVIRONMENT_ID is set (recommended).
#      Its variables are read in memory with `op environment secret list`
#      (1Password CLI 2.42.0+); under WSL the Windows op.exe is used.
#   2. Your shell (or `op run --env-file .sandcastle/op.env -- ...`).
#   3. This file, copied to .sandcastle/secrets.env (gitignored, read only by
#      the host scripts).
# Only the selected agent's one credential is passed into the sandbox.

# 1Password Environment ID: Developer > View Environments > your Environment >
# Manage environment > Copy environment ID. Not a secret, so it can live here.
# Put the keys below (and any SANDCASTLE_* settings) in the Environment itself.
# OP_ENVIRONMENT_ID=
# Optional: path to a specific 1Password CLI binary.
# OP_CLI=

# Default agent: claude | cursor | copilot (or pass --agent).
# SANDCASTLE_AGENT=cursor

# Model overrides per agent (or pass --model).
# SANDCASTLE_CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# SANDCASTLE_CURSOR_MODEL=composer-2.5
# SANDCASTLE_COPILOT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5.5

# Claude: provide one. The OAuth token wins when both are set, unless
# SANDCASTLE_CLAUDE_AUTH=subscription|api forces one.
#   CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN: `claude setup-token` on the host (Pro/Max plan)
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: metered API billing
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# SANDCASTLE_CLAUDE_AUTH=

# Cursor
# CURSOR_API_KEY=

# Copilot: a fine-grained token (github_pat_...) with only the
# "Copilot Requests" permission and no repository access. Classic (ghp_)
# and gh-login (gho_) tokens are refused.
# COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN=
